From 6ea566355d694ef2093459e3dc4256f3b00e4c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:23:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: draw the tab sheet close hand-off copies from the real
 toolbar layout

During the closing cross-fade the parked morph and its icon copies did
not line up with the real toolbar under them, so the icons, the badge,
the favicon and the url text showed twice, at two sizes and a few pixels
apart. The icon copies held only the drawable of the real view, scaled
to fill the whole view box with no padding, scale type or tint, so a
padded toolbar button came out larger than the real icon. Their places
came from rects stored before the sheet opened. The text was laid out by
the pill's own text views (own font metrics, a centred text box, stored
insets), and not the way the real url bar lays it out.

While the close is parked and fading, the drawer now reads the bar from
the live views each frame. The bar rect and url inset are re-read (a bar
that sits more than 16dp from where it rested keeps the stored rect). The
real bar and its icons are shown before anything is measured. Each icon
copy is a bitmap of the real view drawn as it is, with its padding, scale
type, tint and badge, at its size and place; an icon whose view is gone
has no copy. The pill text takes the typeface, font padding, letter
spacing, scale, ellipsis, hint colour and colour spans of the real url
text, the in-flow icons and text margin are cleared, and the text is
moved so its first glyph and baseline are exactly where the real glyphs
are drawn. All of it is undone when the hand-off ends or the sheet opens
again.

The 130 ms fade, the bar band, the page and top toolbar restore, the open
path and the spring are unchanged. The unit tests cover the copy's box
and place (also after a view moved), the text position, the colour
spans, the reset at the end, and a reopen during the fade.
